// Code signing requirements for CameraOverlay.
//
// macOS remembers privacy grants (Camera, etc.) against the app's *designated
// requirement*. With local/ad-hoc signing the default designated requirement
// is derived from the code hash, which changes on every build, so the system
// forgets the camera permission and prompts again on each launch.
//
// Pinning the designated requirement to the bundle identifier keeps it stable
// across rebuilds, so the camera grant is remembered.
//
// Xcode applies these flags to every signing step in the target, including the
// bare debug/preview dylibs nested in the bundle. Those have no Info.plist, so
// the second clause lets them satisfy the requirement too.
designated => identifier "com.abir.CameraOverlay" or !(info [CFBundleIdentifier] exists)
